  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lao People&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s Democratic Republic has ratified 21 ILO Conventions, including all 10 Fundamental Conventions and Convention No. 144 on Tripartite Consultation, reflecting its commitment to international labour standards and social dialogue. Ongoing efforts focus on strengthening implementation and enforcement, including in the areas of freedom of association, collective bargaining, forced labour, child labour and occupational safety and health.

Under the Lao PDR Decent Work Country Programme (DWCP) 2022&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x201c;26, the government and social partners are advancing compliance with ratified Conventions, strengthening labour administration and inspection, and promoting safer workplaces.

Preparation of the next DWCP is underway. A final review workshop is planned for late March or early April 2026, alongside the recruitment of a consultant to support the evaluation and drafting process. Targeted consultations will take place between June and November 2026, with the new DWCP scheduled for launch in the first quarter of 2027, ensuring continued tripartite ownership and alignment with national priorities.</narrative>
  </description>
